#N canvas 20 20 3000 2700 12;
#X text 20 20 c_presence -- ONE DEVICE'S LAST-HEARD CLOCK. It counts ticks since its device last said anything \, declares the device lost when that passes a threshold \, and says so on the presence bus and on err. Instantiated once inside each m_ layer that can be POLLED \, which is why it is a c_ and not a u_: there is more than one \, and the second one is what the prefix exists for., f 84;
#X text 20 190 creation arg 1: the SOURCE NAME \, which is the abstraction's own name -- m_nano \, never nanoKONTROL. REQUIRED. creation arg 2: how many missed ticks count as lost. creation arg 3: the STAGGER in ms \, see below. inlet 1: SEEN -- send it anything at all whenever your device speaks. outlet 1: a bang meaning POLL YOUR DEVICE NOW. outlet 2: presence \, 1 or 0 \, on the transition only., f 84;
#X text 20 370 ⛔ THE SOURCE NAME IS THE ABSTRACTION'S \, NOT THE DEVICE'S \, and that is the m_ boundary rather than a naming preference. Nothing below the m_ layer may know which hardware it is talking to. An abstraction name crossing the bus is exactly what err's SOURCE field already carries \, so this adds no new knowledge to the world -- where publishing nanoKONTROL would., f 84;
#X text 20 550 ⛔ ONLY POLLABLE DEVICES GET ONE OF THESE \, AND A PASSIVE DEVICE MUST NOT AGE. A last-heard clock on a device nobody is touching runs out every time: mother pushes the Organelle's knobs once at load and then says nothing for the rest of the session -- item 237 \, measured -- so an m_organelle that aged would declare itself lost a few seconds into EVERY boot and put a warn on the screen for it. The readout a passive device wants is last-heard \, which is plan-v03.5's diagnostic screen \, not an alarm. Those layers publish expect and seen and instantiate nothing., f 84;
#X text 20 780 ⚠️ THE STAGGER IS NOT COSMETIC. u_present broadcasts ONE tick and every instance hears it in the same logical instant \, so three inquiries would go out together and three replies could come back interleaved BYTE BY BYTE on the single [sysexin] that c_devid reads. Its index would then be counting one device's frame with another's bytes in it. Spacing the outgoing inquiries by tens of milliseconds costs nothing and makes the interleave impossible., f 84;
#X text 20 980 THE COUNTER IS RE-EVALUATED FROM TWO PLACES AND THEY MEET AT THE >= \, which is why seen sends a literal 0 through the test rather than only clearing the store. Clearing the store alone would leave the last computed verdict standing until the next tick \, so a device that came back would stay lost for up to one whole interval and the back message would be late by the same amount., f 84;
#X text 20 1150 ⚠️ [change] IS BARE ON PURPOSE \, WHERE EVERY OTHER ONE IN THIS PATCH CARRIES -1. A bare change starts life holding 0 \, which m_organelle and u_level both have to work around -- and here that is exactly the wanted cold start \, because 0 IS not-lost. The first tick computes 0 \, change swallows it \, and nothing is published until something actually crosses., f 84;
